{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1080508-2e-fan-dark-eras-wolf-and-raven-lodge-of-moon-hounds","id":1080508,"title":"[ 2E fan Dark Eras ] Wolf and Raven - Lodge of Moon-Hounds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-18T13:01:24-07:00","id":1080508,"title":"[ 2E fan Dark Eras ] Wolf and Raven - Lodge of Moon-Hounds","content":"So I have idea for Pure Lodge I my use in my own games, but it's based on W<i>olf and Raven</i> Dark Eras information. Here is quote:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Eras, p.151</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hati, the Hateful One, is viewed as Rabid or Silver Wolf, though their tribes reject Hati\u2019s epithet, <i>M\u00e1nagramr</i> (Moon-Hound)</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading this line I was really strucked why Pure Tribes would not use Hati's epithet. But now I have great idea on their antagonists Lodge. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Basic idea is this - Lodge of Moon-Hounds are Pure extremists that following <i>M\u00e1nagramr,</i> wolf spirit of not sure descendent ( maybe from Rabid or Silver Wolf ). They specialize in hunting Lunes, climbing choirs hierarchy, wanting finally to get to the Mani/Moon himself.<br /> <br /> And so, here is proper Lodge write-up...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://media1.britannica.com/eb-media/35/169935-004-0D0FF099.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Lodge of Moon-Hounds</span></b><br /> <br /> <i>Managarmr</i>. Moon-Hound. It\u2019s title of <i>Hati</i>, monster wolf from Norse myths that is chasing every day <i>M\u00e1ni</i> \u2013 Moon God \u2013 across the sky, to finally get slay at times of Ragnarok. He is patron of the one of most prestigious Lodges of Pure Tribes \u2013 those that hunt the Lunes themselves - Moon Hounds.<br /> <br /> Claiming to hail from Norse mythology, Moon Hounds are relentless in their hunt. Each night, when only Moon is on the sky \u2013 adherents start hunt for first Lune of the Auspice is over their heads. If they get one, they destroy it and by this \u2013 get his Auspice Blessing for the whole Moon Phase. Then they prepare attacks on Forsaken, unsuspecting their enemies have their greatest advantage. Or Moon Hounds track how to get Lune higher in hierarchy, to get information how to strike more lasting blow to Servants of Luna. On day, they say, they will slay Moon itself!<br /> <br /> Of course, only Pure Tribes members are adherents of this Lodge. Most are from children of Silver or Rabid Wolf, but even Predators Kings join group. In the end, what is greatest foe than the Moon Bitch itself? Disturbing for other Anshega is that how easily adherents of Moon Hounds become cursed Bale Hounds, hunting for the Lunes to flayer them with profane <i>Rite of Dead Light</i> ( see<b> Blasphemies</b> for more informarion <i>)</i>. For rest of Lodge this conduct is heresy, letting to life Flayerd Lunes, but local groups of Moon Hounds falls too easily for this trap under right guidance.<br /> <br /> <b>TOTEM: </b><b><i>Managarmr</i></b><br /> Moon Hound is spiritual wolf made of dark clouds. He is said to come from wolf <i>umia</i>, but many point him to be possible <i>magath</i>. Managarmr is somehow demanding patron, calling in the sleep to adherents if they missed one full month without hunting cursed Lunes. He watch over their hunts, often looking as cloud that is overshadowing Moon in last moment before Uratha strikes a Lune \u2013 shutting for few precious seconds his connection to Luna.<br /> <br /> <b>BONDS</b><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Lodge member gains a point of Essence upon seeing the Moon for the first time in a night. If adherent successful hunt the Lune, he can use it\u2019s power as this night Blessing for him \u2013 it works as Forsaken particular Auspice ability, but it\u2019s limited to be usable only once in the same Auspice nights as hunted Lune. If Moon change it\u2019s face to other Auspice, ability is lost till next hunted Lune. For examples, if Moon Hounds get the Ralunim spirit on first night of Full Moon, they can use Rahu Auspice ability for this and two next nights of Full Moon \u2013 but only once.<br /> <br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To foil lunar plot.<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> A Moon Hound must neither deal with nor flee from a Lune.<br /> <br /> <b>SACRED HUNT</b><br /> The Lodge Sacred Hunt grants your character the ability to sense Lunes and gauge their power. He may detect any Lunes within a radius of ten yards per dot of Primal Urge. If he looks at a moon spirit or an individual Ridden by one, he may reflexively learn whatever Dread Powers, Influences, Manifestations, and Numina are at its disposal. An adherent who encounters Forsaken during the Sacred Hunt may also perceive the extent of Luna's blessing upon them. By looking upon one of the Urdaga, he may reflexively identify his Auspice and the number of Moon Gift Facets engraved upon him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-24-2017, 02:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T13:49:48-07:00","id":1080535,"title":"","content":"Oooh.<br /> <br /> They have the same sacred prey as my Sun Walkers Lodge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T23:53:37-07:00","id":1080764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1080508-2e-fan-dark-eras-wolf-and-raven-lodge-of-moon-hounds?p=1080535#post1080535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oooh.<br /> <br /> They have the same sacred prey as my Sun Walkers Lodge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great ( Pure ) minds think the same way! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Lodge of Moon-Hounds will be much more relic of older times, when many Pure literally think their Totems chased Mani on the skies. <br /> <br /> But I will check your Lodge for inspirations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T12:32:28-07:00","id":1096000,"title":"","content":"Added Lodges write-up to opening post. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a>, I took some parts from yours Sun Walkers write-up, as Sacred Prey of both Lodges is very same - and they are similar in some other ways. I hope you are not angry because of that.<br /> <br /> I'm just thinking what Lodge Merits and Tools would have sense for my Moon Hounds - any ideas you got?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T13:52:07-07:00","id":1096020,"title":"","content":"Well, I see some similarities, but they're still distinct from my Sun Walkers nonetheless. Nice work adapting the bits and pieces you took to your Lodge.<br /> x3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T14:33:15-07:00","id":1096030,"title":"","content":"This is nice. Any chance they're associated with our favorite not-Tribe, the Bale Hounds, through things like Rite of the Flayed Lune? (not sure if this is the right name)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T23:27:20-07:00","id":1096179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1080508-2e-fan-dark-eras-wolf-and-raven-lodge-of-moon-hounds?p=1096030#post1096030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any chance they're associated with our favorite not-Tribe, the Bale Hounds, through things like Rite of the Flayed Lune? (not sure if this is the right name)</div> </div> </div> </div>Rite is called <i>Rite of Dead Light</i> in <b>Blasphemies</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And Moon Hounds were <i>envisioned</i> for being corrupted by the Bale Hounds. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I got idea on them by reading<i> Wolf &amp; Raven</i> and <i>Blasphemies</i> in near the same time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I shall mark the high number of Bale Hounds heresy in their ranks in Lodge write-up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-24-2017, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T13:23:37-07:00","id":1217093,"title":"","content":"\u200bThinking on some NPCs from this Lodge, got idea to write the Managarmr as Spirit to use in your games. Hopes it looks cool and as good Rank 5 being. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><i>Managarmr</i> \u2013 Moon Hound</b></span><br /> <br /> <b><i>\u2018&lt;Howl at the Moon in the sky&gt;\u2019</i></b><br /> <br /> Moon Hound is spiritual wolf made of dark clouds. He is said to come from wolf <i>umia</i>, but many point him to be possible <i>magath</i>. Managarmr watch over hunts of his adherents, often looking as cloud that is overshadowing Moon in last moment before Uratha strikes a Lune \u2013 shutting for few precious seconds his connection to Luna. There is rumor he is Secondborn of Silver or Dire Wolf \u2013 and he personally remember what Moon did at the moment of Urfarah\u2019s death.<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> Managarmr looks like a wolf made of living, breathing dark cloud. Temperature around him drops a few degrees and air is electric, like jest before the storm. His eyes are two sparks of lighting for brewing storm \u2013 that becomes whole thunder cascades if he is furious. And often he is.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints: </b>Moon Hound has only one real goal \u2013 to kill the Moon. And he takes it literally. He can be appease by giving Lunes as sacrifices to him. But he will do anything to finally get his teeth on Luna \u2013 even if that would mean his end. Of course, he much more want to win, so he looks for strategies and weakness to get his final blow.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank:</b> 5<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 15, Finesse 9, Resistance 12<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 50<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 24<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 9<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 31<br /> <b>Size:</b> 4 ( Can assume form of Dark Cloud \u2013 then Size 40? )<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 16 ( In Cloud form \u2013 52 )<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Weather \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Wolf \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, Blast ( Lighting ), Implant Mission, Innocuous ( As Cloud ), Path Finder, Regenerate, Seek, Speed, Sign, Telekinesis ( \u2018Smart\u2019 Wind )<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Dark Cloud*, Discorporate, Gauntlet Breach, Image, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Cannot show weakness to Luna and it\u2019s kind<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Silver dust spread into air on direct moonlight<br /> <br /> *<b>Manifestation \u2013 Dark Cloud</b><br /> Spirit can become living part of Shadow Realm ( or Physical ) sky. It stretches and assumes much larger Size \u2013 but is treated as in Twilight Form to any powers that cannot attack him in this stretched shape at once. Exception is Bane, that works even on tiniest part of Dark Cloud on contact. In this form, being is also assumed to fly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}